Demo_1.3A_SQLLite_Read_from_db_JavaConfig
=====================================
Requirement: 
	From MySQL Database Pump the Data of Employees  to an XML file.
	use SQLLite as Job Repo /MetaData Database
	
Pre-requisite:
	Execute Employee.sql file script in MySQL database.
	
Observations:
 1) Open pom.xml file and observe the dependencies
 2) Observe SpringBatchConfig.java class for Spring batch configuration.
 3) Open UITester, Observe that AnnotationConfigApplicationContext(SpringBatchConfig.class) is used.  	
 4) Run the UITester main class, and Observe that output.xml created inside the xml folder	
 [Note: xml folder and output.xml file can be deleted. Both will be created on execution]
 
Notes:

	Heart of Spring Batch is a job. 
	Job is template which tells how batch processing has to be performed.
	Job has following:
		Instances(logical run of a job is called job instance)
		JobExecution(attempt to run a job )
		ExecutionContext
		Parameters
	Steps 1 or more, a job can have one more steps)
		They define a phase of processing (reading, processing, writing )
		spring-batch-reference-model.png
	StepExecution
 
 
Versions:
	Spring Batch	: 4.3.4
	Spring 		 		: 5.3.14
	MySQL 			: 8.0.19
	
